# Cloudflare Pages redirects — the aihu.dev IA move.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. apps/docs (the site aihu.dev serves today) prerenders
# to `dist/<slug>/index.html`, so every one of its slugs is a LIVE URL: it is in
# the published sitemap.xml, in llms.txt, and in each page's own `canonical`.
# The rebuilt docs app reorganised the IA — packages/* became api/*, and the three
# top-level entry pages moved under guides/ — so without these rules the
# cutover turns ~27 advertised URLs into 404s.
#
# Only genuinely MOVED paths are listed. Every guide that kept its path
# (/guides/reactivity, /guides/theming, /guides/styling, …) needs no rule and
# has none — a redirect from a path to itself is a loop.
#
# Verified before writing: every target on the right-hand side resolves to a
# real prerendered page in the docs app. Checked mechanically against the built
# page list, not by eye.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. 301 throughout — these moves are permanent, and
# a 301 is what transfers link equity and gets cached by crawlers.

# ── The package reference: /packages/* → /api/* ──────────────────────────────
# A splat rather than 22 literal rules. Confirmed that all 22 slugs apps/docs
# published (adapter-cloudflare, adapter-vercel, agent-a2a, agent-acp,
# agent-server, ai, auth, cli, context, editor, language-server, magna, mcp,
# plugin-drizzle, plugin-kindly-note, reactive, seo, store, tsc, ui,
# use) exist under /api/. This app publishes 40 api pages, so the splat also
# catches any old deep link to a package the old site never had a page for —
# which lands on a real page rather than a 404.
/packages/*                 /api/:splat                 301

# ── Entry pages that moved under /guides/ ────────────────────────────────────
/introduction               /                           301
/installation               /guides/installation        301
/getting-started            /guides/getting-started     301
/migration                  /guides/migration           301

# ── The reference index ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/api-reference              /api                        301

# ── Carried over from apps/docs/public/_redirects ────────────────────────────
# The old site shipped exactly one rule, `/docs → /docs/introduction`. Its
# target no longer exists (and `/docs/*` was never a prefix this app serves),
# so it is retargeted to the new home of the introduction content rather than
# dropped: anything still linking /docs deserves a landing, not a 404.
/docs                       /                           301
